<!-- CELLCLOCK -->
<section id="cellclock" class="feat">
  <div class="feat-in">
    <div class="center reveal">
      <div class="badge">An Idea I Want To Build · Biology</div>
      <h2 class="ftitle">CellClock</h2>
      <div class="fsub">Can we reprogram how long a cell lives?</div>
    </div>

    <div class="why reveal">
      <div class="kicker">Why I want to build this</div>
      <p>I became obsessed with one question at 3am: can you change how long a cell lives by rewriting the genetic circuit that runs its internal clock? It sounds like science fiction. It isn't. In 2023, a team published a result in <em>Science</em> — they engineered a genetic toggle into yeast and extended its replicative lifespan by <strong>82%</strong>. I read it and I could not stop thinking about it.</p>
      <p>So I want to build it — a home-lab version, with tools I can actually get my hands on: GFP-tagged yeast carrying a synthetic genetic oscillator, watched cell by cell through automated microscopy, with AI doing the image analysis no human has the patience for. CellClock is the smallest possible version of the thing I want to spend my life on — a <em>longevity research network</em> where compute and biology stop being treated as separate disciplines.</p>
      <p>Aging is not one disease. It is a process — and processes can be reprogrammed. I am not naïve about the distance between a yeast cell and a human being; it is enormous. But every important thing starts with someone deciding the question is worth asking out loud, in a real experiment, with real cells. <strong>This is the experiment I most want to start.</strong></p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid2 reveal">
      <div class="cell"><div class="l">The Question</div><div class="x">Can we reprogram how long a cell lives by engineering the genetic circuits that control its internal clock?</div></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="l">The Method</div><div class="x">GFP-tagged yeast with a synthetic genetic oscillator, tracked via automated microscopy and AI-driven image analysis over time.</div></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="l">The Vision</div><div class="x">A closed-loop system where AI observes, analyzes, and eventually guides biological intervention autonomously — bringing compute to biology.</div></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="l">The Connection</div><div class="x">The same principle behind NeuroBridge — efficient, adaptive computation — applied to understanding how living systems age and adapt.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="tags reveal">
      <span class="tag">S. cerevisiae</span><span class="tag">CRISPR</span><span class="tag">GFP</span><span class="tag">OpenCV</span><span class="tag">Synthetic Biology</span><span class="tag">Longevity</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fcta reveal"><a href="https://github.com/Reverie-Co" class="btn btn-green" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow the experiment &#8599;</a></div>
